info title=Thalassa Mooring
info author=Custom Islands
info description=The Network's surface station: a steel deck over a moonpool, a crane and a diving bell that rides 20 m down, a water tower and a vending machine. The fifth island of The Sunken Kingdom.
island on.arrive=message||A crane over a steel deck - and under it, a square of black water going straight down.

note handbook Station handbook | THALASSA MOORING - HANDBOOK (annotated by the last crew)\n\n1. Fresh water from the tower. Pipes to the deck. Don't drink from the moonpool. ("Kowalski.")\n2. The purifier plans are in the office. Keep the filters dry.\n3. The bell: stand on it, use it. It goes down the shaft to the shelf at twenty metres and comes back when used again.\n4. Tokens for the machine - the old crews hid them round the decks, like squirrels with a pension.\n5. Nobody goes below the shelf edge. Nobody.\n\nPencilled over rule 5, in a different hand: "Unless the Spire sends you. Then everybody does, and nobody comes back."
note towerchest Water tower chest | A chest on top of the water tower: water tank plans.
note pipecrate Pipe crate | A crate of pipe fittings: water pipe plans.
note officechest Station office chest | The office chest: electric purifier plans and a logbook stub.
note storeshed Store shed chest | The store shed's chest: large storage plans.
loot towerchest Blueprint_WaterTank*1;Plank*4
prop towerchest loot.refill=0
loot pipecrate Blueprint_Pipe_Water*1;Scrap*3
prop pipecrate loot.refill=0
loot officechest Blueprint_ElectricPurifier*1;Bolt*2
prop officechest loot.refill=0
loot storeshed Blueprint_Storage_Large*1;Plank*6;Nail*10
prop storeshed loot.refill=0

prop deckzone zone.id=deck
prop deckzone zone.radius=5
prop deckzone zone.message=Thalassa Mooring's deck. The moonpool breathes cold air.
prop bell obj.name=bell
prop bell beh.use=Ride the diving bell
prop bell beh.move=0,-20,0
prop bell beh.moveTime=12
prop bell beh.carry=1
prop bell on.use=switch|\nmessage||The crane's winch groans. The bell sinks into the shaft.
prop bellzone zone.id=bell
prop bellzone zone.radius=4
prop bellzone zone.air=1
prop bellzone zone.repeat=1
prop bellzone zone.message=Twenty metres down. Through the shaft's mouth: a glowing shelf, lamps in a line - the shelf the handbook spoke of.
prop bellbub atmo.particles=bubbles
prop bellbub zone.radius=3
prop bellcrane obj.name=bellcrane

note th_cavechest Bell crew's locker | A bell crew locker: a dive knife's sheath, a rope, a tin of grease.
loot th_cavechest Rope*3;Bolt*2;Leather*1;Copper*2
prop th_cavechest loot.refill=0
note th_ruinnote Dive log | DIVE LOG - DIVE MASTER R. OYELARAN\n\nDive 41: east of the station, off the rocks. Order from the Spire: cut the trench cable at marker 3. Diver did not surface. Her sample bag is still down there, buried in the sand.\nDive 44: north-east, by the old marker. Order from the Spire: cut the dome feed. Line cut - not by us.\nDive 47: south, past the dinghy. Order from the Spire: cut the lab line. Bell came up empty.\nThree dives, three cables, three crews. Why is the Director cutting his own Network? He says "to keep the Commons quiet". Quiet from what?\nWhoever has a metal detector: their tags will ring under the sand. Bring them home.
note th_wrecknote Dinghy logbook | DINGHY LOGBOOK\n\nTook the dinghy out for dive 47. Came back without the bell crew. I tied her up on the rocks, walked to the hut, and sat on the floor for a long time.\nThen a gardener rowed in from Biome Seven with a diver, an old man and a hen, and the hen walked straight into my hut as if it had paid rent.\nThe diver, Marlowe, asked about the shuttle. I told her what we heard on the station set: the shuttle hit the reef past the Caisson Yard, and the children walked. Then I told her what the dive orders were. She went very quiet. She said she used to lay those cables.
note th_wreckcrate Dinghy stores | The dinghy's stores crate: spare line, a lamp, a tin of fuel.
loot th_wreckcrate Rope*3;Plank*3;Scrap*2;Battery*1
prop th_wreckcrate loot.refill=0

# --- DEEP 1-HOUR (10-24): story items, notes and checks
story th_key|Salvage store key|Hinge|The salvage store's key, from the harbour master's locker on Mooring Hill.
story sk_crest|Kingdom crest shard|Bolt|A shard of the Sunken Kingdom's crest, from a drowned building. The Hollow's crown vault wants nine.
note thdeep Salvage store chest | The salvage crew's chest: their pay and a crest shard.
loot thdeep story:sk_crest*1;MetalIngot*2;Bolt*3;OxygenBottle*1;TradeToken*2
prop thdeep if.open=has|story:th_key|1
prop thdeep else.open=message||Locked. A tag: "Key in my locker on Mooring Hill. - Harbour master".
prop thdeep loot.refill=0
note thlocker Mooring hill locker | The harbour master's locker: the salvage store key.
loot thlocker story:th_key*1;MetalIngot*3;CopperIngot*2;Rope*3;Cooked_Potato*2
prop thlocker loot.refill=0
note thsumnote Harbour master's card | MOORING HILL - HARBOUR MASTER\n\nFrom here I watched the bell go down every morning, and every evening I counted heads coming up. Then the Spire's dive orders started, and I stopped counting, because the numbers were wrong.\nI have locked the salvage store and put its key in my locker here, so nobody else goes down for the Director's cables.\nIf you must go down: the crew's pump on the pit rim sends air down the hose to the first floor. Work it first. Breathe on the way.\nAnd if anybody asks, I was never here. I was fishing.
note thbldnote Ines's slate (salvage store) | DIVE SLATE - I. MARLOWE, SALVAGE STORE\n\nMilo. The station diver showed me their orders. Cut the cables. All of them. Signed "Sealkeeper".\nI laid those cables, love. With your dad. They carried the lights from the Spire to the domes and the labs and the Commons. Someone cut the lights off from the Commons on purpose, and the Commons is where everybody went.\nI am going down the bell to the shelf. The survey team strung lamps along the shelf edge to the Yard, and the radio says the Yard road still has light. Teo says he will wait here and look after the hen, which is his way of saying his knees have had enough.\nDown the bell. Then the shelf. Then you.
note thledge Lookout's cache | A harbour lookout's cache on a ledge.
loot thledge Rope*3;Bolt*2;Feather*3
prop thledge loot.refill=0
note thcave2chest Salvager's spare chest | A salvager's spare chest in the south rock.
loot thcave2chest CopperOre*3;Rope*2;Battery*1
prop thcave2chest loot.refill=0
prop thsummit zone.id=th_summit
prop thsummit zone.radius=2.5
prop thsummit zone.message=The top of Mooring Hill. The whole island lies below.
story th_pump|Air line running|Pump|The salvage pump is running: air down the hose into the flooded store.
prop thpump obj.name=thpump
prop thpump beh.use=Work the salvage pump
prop thpump if.use=!signal|thpump
prop thpump on.use=signal||thpump\nshow|thair1\nshow|thbub1\nshow|thair2\nshow|thbub2\nhide|thwater\ngive||story:th_pump*1\nmessage||The pump thumps into life. Down in the pit, bubbles stream out of the store's windows: air in there now.
prop thair1 obj.name=thair1
prop thair1 zone.id=th_air1
prop thair1 zone.radius=2.2
prop thair1 zone.repeat=1
prop thair1 zone.air=1
prop thair1 zone.message=The pump's air, trapped under the first floor ceiling. Breathe.
prop thair1 beh.hidden=1
prop thair2 obj.name=thair2
prop thair2 zone.id=th_air2
prop thair2 zone.radius=2.2
prop thair2 zone.repeat=1
prop thair2 zone.air=1
prop thair2 zone.message=Air from the hose, by the ground floor chest. Breathe.
prop thair2 beh.hidden=1
prop thbub1 atmo.particles=bubbles
prop thbub1 zone.radius=3
prop thbub1 beh.hidden=1
prop thbub2 atmo.particles=bubbles
prop thbub2 zone.radius=3
prop thbub2 beh.hidden=1
prop thwater obj.name=thwater
prop thwater zone.id=thwater
prop thwater zone.radius=9
prop thwater zone.hazard=deep
prop thwater zone.damage=1
prop thwater zone.safe=none
prop thwater zone.hazardMsg=Cold, deep water: your breath goes fast down here. The salvage pump on the rim would help.

quest title=The Surface Station
quest intro=Wren's boat brought Ines and Teo to this surface station. Find its deck.
step reach|deck|1|Climb onto the station's deck
step read|Station handbook|1|Read the station handbook
step blueprint|Blueprint_WaterTank|1|Climb the water tower: water tank plans
step blueprint|Blueprint_Pipe_Water|1|Find the water pipe plans in the pipe crate
step blueprint|Blueprint_ElectricPurifier|1|Find the purifier plans in the station office
step blueprint|Blueprint_Storage_Large|1|Open the store shed: large storage plans
step read|Dive log|1|Read the dive log in the dive master's hut in the north
step read|Dinghy logbook|1|Read the logbook at the divers' dinghy in the south-west
step reach|th_summit|1|Climb Mooring Hill to the harbour master's tower
step collect|story:th_key|1|Take the salvage store key from the harbour master's locker
step collect|story:th_pump|1|Work the salvage pump on the pit rim to send air down to the flooded store
step open|Salvage store chest|1|Dive down the air line into the salvage store and unlock its chest
step read|Ines's slate (salvage store)|1|Read the diver's slate in the salvage store
step reach|bell|1|Ride the diving bell 20 m down the shaft after her
quest done=The Spire ordered its own cables cut. Down the shaft the shelf glows; the Receiver picks up the survey lamps on band 600.
quest reward=Rope*4;Plank*6

save Thalassa Mooring
